id: decisions/042-numbers-on-inferred-only
title: "Where a number may carry uncertainty"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'confidence-representation'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: confidence-representation
axis_gloss: "whether uncertainty is carried as a number or score, or left as an unnumbered qualitative judgment"
poles:
  a: unquantified-judgment
  b: quantified-confidence
split: genuinely-split
draft_status: full
leverage: 6
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(6) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1)"

question: >
  When a bot or record carries uncertainty, should it carry a number that can be
  computed over, or a qualitative judgment in prose, and if a number, must the
  number leave the calculation into the receipt?

why_it_matters: >
  Nothing authored settles this: next-move-logic computes a score and outputs
  prose, q-space weights eleven terms with no prose ranking them, and one
  example puts confidence only on inferred items. Once answered, a bot that
  scores a move knows whether the score is evidence it must show or scaffolding
  it must hide, and a child Yawn learns whether a number on a claim is
  inspectable or off limits.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    2 judgments sit at unquantified-judgment (0 authored) and 4 at
    quantified-confidence (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave stands behind the q-space frontier_score weights as a ranking he
    means, or regards them as a placeholder formula.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Uncertainty is carried qualitatively, as epistemic_status plus
      epistemic_note. Scores and weights are internal scaffolding and never appear
      in outputs, receipts or records.
    cost: "Strip confidence: from examples/dave-good-dad-objective-holon.yawn; q-space/protocol-v1.yawn frontier_score becomes an implementation detail with no record of which formula ran."
    risk: "A move chosen by a score cannot be replayed, against yawn.yawn's inspectable, correctable, replayable."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that rejects confidence: or score: keys in records/ and examples/."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0118"
      - "J0846"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Uncertainty is carried as a number wherever a claim is inferred, and
      every score or weight that decides a move or ranking is written into the
      receipt so it can be inspected and replayed.
    cost: "core/next-move-logic.yawn output gains a score field; every scored selection writes the number and the formula id; reported and observed items may also carry numbers."
    risk: "Numbers on reported items imply a precision nobody measured; a number is read as authority, which the constitution forbids (confidence cannot ratify an objective)."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend scripts/validate-inquiry-selection-receipt-v0.1.mjs and scripts/validate-orientation-map-v0.1.mjs to require score and formula version on any receipt derived from a scored selection."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0394"
      - "J1040"
      - "J1041"
      - "J1042"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: A number may attach only to an item whose epistemic_status is inferred
      or predicted; reported and observed items carry none. Any score that decides a
      move or ranking is written into the receipt with the formula id and version,
      so the number is inspectable, and no number ratifies anything, per the
      constitution.
    cost: "core/next-move-logic.yawn output gains score and formula fields; q-space/protocol-v1.yawn frontier_score gets a version id; a check that confidence: sits only beside inferred or predicted."
    risk: "Every inferred item sprouts a number of no provenance because the rule allows it."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that confidence: appears only next to epistemic_status inferred or predicted; extend scripts/validate-inquiry-selection-receipt-v0.1.mjs to require score and formula id on scored receipts."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0394"
      - "J0118"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.55
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Genuinely open: none of the six judgments is authored and none has proof
    beyond seed-backed. The closest thing to a rule is J0394's pattern, numbers
    only on inferred items, which is coherent with the enforced seven-value
    epistemic vocabulary. The strongest argument against A is the canonical
    sentence: a score that never leaves the calculation (J0118) is not inspectable
    or replayable. The strongest argument against B is the constitution's
    'confidence cannot ratify an objective', which C writes in as a boundary on
    any number. Close; the executable backing that exists (the inquiry-selection
    receipt validator) is where C would land first.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "One record states where numbers may appear and that no number ratifies a move or an objective."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects confidence: on items whose epistemic_status is reported or observed, and passes."
    - "core/next-move-logic.yawn output either carries the score and formula id or states why it must not."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A receipt names its chosen move 'because score' with no number in it, or a
    number appears beside a reported item and the suite stays green.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0118"
  - "J0846"
  - "J0394"
  - "J1040"
  - "J1041"
  - "J1042"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
